          <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(32px, 3.2vw, 40px); line-height: 1">Building With AI</h2>
          <a href="/endurance-grid/" style="background: #4AB8D4; color: #0E0E10; font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; padding: 16px 26px; border-radius: 12px">See How I Built Endurance Grid</a>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 999 1 min(100%, 480px); min-width: 0">
          <p style="margin: 0 0 18px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #D8E3E8">At Elate, I led the AI product line and shipped four AI modules built on Gemini models: <a href="https://www.goelate.com/ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #4AB8D4; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px">Strategy Advisor</a>, <a href="https://www.goelate.com/ai/plan-analyzer" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #4AB8D4; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px">Plan Analyzer</a>, <a href="https://www.goelate.com/ai/risk-navigator" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #4AB8D4; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px">Risk Navigator</a>, and <a href="https://www.goelate.com/ai/reporting-assistant" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #4AB8D4; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px">Reporting Assistant</a>.</p>
          <p style="margin: 0 0 18px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #D8E3E8">In June, I started building Endurance Grid with AI coding agents. Today it's a website with 5–10K monthly visitors (depending on the month) plus iOS and Android apps on one shared backend. The mobile apps are live in the App Store and Google Play. The app went from its first line of code to both stores in about three and a half months.</p>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #D8E3E8">I research the problems to solve, design what gets built and how it fits our product strategy, build it, and set up the AI rules that keep the work reliable.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr)); gap: 16px">
        <div style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1C1C1E; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; border-top: 6px solid #4AB8D4">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 10px; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 22px">Research and Design First</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #444444">Every feature starts with the user problem and a clickable design. AI speeds up the build, but it doesn't decide what to build.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1C1C1E; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; border-top: 6px solid #4AB8D4">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 10px; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 22px">Written Rules for the Agents</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #444444">When an agent makes a mistake, it becomes a rule, so it doesn't happen twice. The rules cover the database, security, and releases.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1C1C1E; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; border-top: 6px solid #4AB8D4">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 10px; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 22px">Nothing Ships Unchecked</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #444444">Every change runs automated tests and checks before it can merge. Automated and manual testing help improve the user experience and reduce downtime.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1C1C1E; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; border-top: 6px solid #4AB8D4">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 10px; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 22px">Built Responsibly</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #444444">Security reviews, an incident runbook, product analytics, and monitoring. Customer trust and a good security posture are critical to building.</p>
